## Current behavior

Just like [`nestjs/graphql`](https://github.com/nestjs/graphql/blob/master/lib/graphql.module.ts), people are doing fancy scanning to load specific classes (using `MetadataScanner` and `modulesContainer `), I don't think this is the best way to achieve this purpose. When you have a big project and several modules doing this scanning, your boss will be pissed off.

This is a huge waste of performance!


## Expected behavior (proposal)

So could we have add two things:

1. An new array to Module that tells Nest these are `Autoload Handlers`.
2. A decorator that tells Nest this is a class needs to be handled by some `Autoload Handler`.

Because Nest itself have to traverse all modules (and providers) by design, when it sees this decorator, it just store them; when traversing finished, it will process them at once. 

Maybe looks like this:

`my-resolver.resolver.ts`

```typescript
import { Autoload, Injectable } from 'nestjs/nest';
import { AUTOLOAD_MY_MODULE } from './my-autoloader.autoloader';

@Injectable()
@Autoload(AUTOLOAD_MY_MODULE)
export class MyResolver {
  // ...
}
```

`my-autoloader.autoloader.ts`

```typescript
import { Autoloader } from 'nestjs/common';
import { HandleAutoload } from 'nestjs/interfaces';

const AUTOLOAD_MY_MODULE = '__ AUTOLOAD_MY_MODULE__';

@Autoloader(AUTOLOAD_MY_MODULE)
export class MyAutoloader implements HandleAutoload {
  handleAutoload(instance, classRef) { }
}
```

`my-module.module.ts`

```typescript
// ...

@Module({
  //...
  'autoloader': [
    MyAutoloader,
  ],
})
export class MyModule {
  // ...
}
```


## Minimal reproduction of the problem with instructions

See above.


## What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?

The future of `Nest`.


